@model ReformedHistory.Views.Content.Confessions.Secret.SecretSection

<h2 id="@this.Model.Link">Chapter @this.Model.Index</h2>
<h3>@this.Model.Name</h3>
<br />

<div class="centerQuote">
    <span>
        So long as we are without Christ and separated from him, nothing which he suffered and did for 
        the salvation of the human race is of the least benefit to us. To communicate to us the blessings 
        which he received from the Father, he must become ours and dwell in us.
    </span>
    <span>John Calvin, Institutes of the Christian Religion</span>
</div>
    
<ol>
    <li>
        God reveals His design and purpose for the church in His covenant, which is fulfilled in the person
        and work of Jesus Christ. Christ is the sum and substance of the covenant: everyone in the covenant
        is united to Christ, and everyone united to Christ is in the covenant. Christ is in his people, and they
        are in Him. He is the vine, and they the branches.
    </li>
    <li>
        This mystical union is formed by a loving bond of faith between a person and Christ, and it
        is nourished and sustained through the work of the Holy Spirit. In no other way can man apprehend 
        Christ but through faith alone.
    </li>
    <li>
        All evangelical graces and benefits of Christ, including the forgiveness of sins, justification, 
        sanctification, and communion, flow outwardly from this mystical union. A person cannot be forgiven
        in themself, but only by Christ and through Christ. Likewise nobody may be justified apart from 
        being taken up and participating in Christ's justification.
    </li>
    <li>
        Should anybody be downcast and in need of assurance, they need only look to Christ: Christ in His
        sacraments, Christ in His church, Christ in His victory over death, and Christ living with us.
    </li>
</ol>
<br />